package Libraries.Game.Graphics.Models.Data

use Libraries.Compute.Vector3
use Libraries.Game.Graphics.Color

/*
ModelLightData holds one light read from a model file, such as a lamp's
bulb in a glTF file that uses the KHR_lights_punctual extension. A Model
loaded from such a file turns each of these into a PointLight, SpotLight or
DirectionalLight (Lighting plan L8).

The position and direction are in the model's own space, the same space
its meshes are in, so a light placed on a lamp's bulb in the file lands on
the bulb in the loaded model. Area lights in a file are read as point
lights. Ambient lights are not read.

The color is kept with its brightest part at 1, and the strength is kept
separately as the intensity, as it was in the file (candela for point and
spot lights in glTF, lux for directional lights).
*/
class ModelLightData
    // The kinds of light a file can hold (Lighting plan L8).
    public constant integer POINT = 0
    public constant integer DIRECTIONAL = 1
    public constant integer SPOT = 2

    /*
    How many units of Quorum light intensity one unit of a file light's
    intensity becomes (Lighting plan L8). Quorum's lighting divides a point
    light's color times intensity by the distance squared and uses the
    albedo over pi for diffuse light, as the glTF lights extension expects,
    so a glTF light in candela (point and spot) or lux (directional) is used
    as it is. Unsure: files exported from Blender often have large values,
    and how they look also depends on the layer's exposure.
    */
    public constant number INTENSITY_SCALE = 1.0

    integer type = 0
    text name = ""
    Color color
    number intensity = 0
    number range = 0
    number innerAngle = 0
    number outerAngle = 45
    Vector3 position
    Vector3 direction

    on create
        color:SetColor(1, 1, 1, 1)
        direction:Set(0, 0, -1)
    end

    /*
    This action returns the kind of light: POINT, DIRECTIONAL or SPOT
    (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Returns The kind of light.
    */
    action GetType returns integer
        return type
    end

    /*
    This action sets the kind of light: POINT, DIRECTIONAL or SPOT
    (Lighting plan L8). Any other value is treated as POINT.

    Attribute: Parameter type The kind of light.
    */
    action SetType(integer type)
        if type = DIRECTIONAL or type = SPOT
            me:type = type
        else
            me:type = POINT
        end
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the light is a point light (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Returns True for a point light.
    */
    action IsPointLight returns boolean
        return type = POINT
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the light is a directional light, like the
    sun (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Returns True for a directional light.
    */
    action IsDirectionalLight returns boolean
        return type = DIRECTIONAL
    end

    /*
    This action returns true if the light is a spot light (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Returns True for a spot light.
    */
    action IsSpotLight returns boolean
        return type = SPOT
    end

    /*
    This action returns the light's name, as it is in the file (Lighting
    plan L8). For glTF files, this is the name of the node the light is on.

    Attribute: Returns The light's name.
    */
    action GetName returns text
        return name
    end

    /*
    This action sets the light's name (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Parameter name The light's name.
    */
    action SetName(text name)
        if name = undefined
            me:name = ""
        else
            me:name = name
        end
    end

    /*
    This action returns the light's color, with its brightest part at 1
    (Lighting plan L8). Change it with SetColor.

    Attribute: Returns The light's color.
    */
    action GetColor returns Color
        return color
    end

    /*
    This action sets the light's color from its red, green and blue parts,
    each from 0 to 1 (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Parameter red The red part.
    Attribute: Parameter green The green part.
    Attribute: Parameter blue The blue part.
    */
    action SetColor(number red, number green, number blue)
        color:SetColor(red, green, blue, 1)
    end

    /*
    This action returns how bright the light is, as it was in the file
    (Lighting plan L8). For glTF, this is in candela for point and spot
    lights, and lux for directional lights.

    Attribute: Returns The light's intensity in the file's units.
    */
    action GetIntensity returns number
        return intensity
    end

    /*
    This action sets how bright the light is, in the file's units (Lighting
    plan L8). A value below 0 is kept as 0.

    Attribute: Parameter intensity The light's intensity.
    */
    action SetIntensity(number intensity)
        if intensity < 0
            me:intensity = 0
        else
            me:intensity = intensity
        end
    end

    /*
    This action returns how bright the light is in Quorum's units: the
    file's intensity times INTENSITY_SCALE (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Returns The intensity to give a Quorum light.
    */
    action GetQuorumIntensity returns number
        return intensity * INTENSITY_SCALE
    end

    /*
    This action returns how far the light reaches, or 0 if the file did not
    say (Lighting plan L8). Directional lights have no range.

    Attribute: Returns The light's range, in the model's units, or 0.
    */
    action GetRange returns number
        return range
    end

    /*
    This action sets how far the light reaches, or 0 if the file did not
    say (Lighting plan L8). A value below 0 is kept as 0.

    Attribute: Parameter range The light's range, or 0.
    */
    action SetRange(number range)
        if range < 0
            me:range = 0
        else
            me:range = range
        end
    end

    /*
    This action returns a spot light's inner angle, in degrees, measured
    from the direction it points: inside it, the light is at full strength
    (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Returns The inner angle, in degrees.
    */
    action GetInnerAngle returns number
        return innerAngle
    end

    /*
    This action returns a spot light's outer angle, in degrees, measured
    from the direction it points: past it, the light gives no light
    (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Returns The outer angle, in degrees.
    */
    action GetOuterAngle returns number
        return outerAngle
    end

    /*
    This action sets a spot light's inner and outer angles, in degrees,
    each measured from the direction it points (Lighting plan L8).

    Attribute: Parameter inner The angle of full strength, in degrees.
    Attribute: Parameter outer The angle where the light ends, in degrees.
    */
    action SetConeAngles(number inner, number outer)
        innerAngle = inner
        outerAngle = outer
    end

    /*
    This action returns where the light is, in the model's own space
    (Lighting plan L8). Change it with SetPosition.

    Attribute: Returns The light's position.
    */
    action GetPosition returns Vector3
        return position
    end

    /*
    This action sets where the light is, in the model's own space (Lighting
    plan L8).

    Attribute: Parameter x The position along x.
    Attribute: Parameter y The position along y.
    Attribute: Parameter z The position along z.
    */
    action SetPosition(number x, number y, number z)
        position:Set(x, y, z)
    end

    /*
    This action returns the direction the light shines, in the model's own
    space, of length 1 (Lighting plan L8). Point lights ignore it. Change it
    with SetDirection.

    Attribute: Returns The light's direction.
    */
    action GetDirection returns Vector3
        return direction
    end

    /*
    This action sets the direction the light shines, in the model's own
    space (Lighting plan L8). It is made length 1. A direction of zero
    length is ignored.

    Attribute: Parameter x The direction along x.
    Attribute: Parameter y The direction along y.
    Attribute: Parameter z The direction along z.
    */
    action SetDirection(number x, number y, number z)
        number lengthSquared = x * x + y * y + z * z
        if lengthSquared < 0.000000000001
            return now
        end
        direction:Set(x, y, z)
        direction:Normalize()
    end
end
